# Anchored to the root on purpose. A bare `docs/` matches a directory at ANY depth,
# and there are three in this tree: this one, which holds audits, remediation plans
# and handoff notes that are working documents rather than course material, plus
# `src/workshops/assistant/{before,after}/docs/`, which hold the student-facing
# release-evidence checklist. Seven places inside `src/` point at that checklist —
# both Makefiles, `release.py`'s own failure message, two READMEs — and it was
# ignored, so it never shipped, and every one of those references dangled in the
# released ZIP. `check-doc-links.mjs` now fails the build if that recurs.
#
# `/docs/*` and not `/docs/`, because git does not descend into an excluded
# directory and a negation cannot reach inside one — ignoring the directory makes
# the `!` line below silently do nothing. Ignoring the *entries* leaves the
# directory itself readable, so the exception applies.
/docs/*
# The one exception, because it is a runbook rather than a finding: it is the
# maintainer's release order, `e2e.yml` cites it for the gate it cannot run
# itself, and it is the only file under `/docs/` that anything outside `/docs/`
# points at — the other fourteen are audits and plans with no inbound references.
!/docs/RELEASE-CHECKLIST.md

# pnpm
.pnpm-store/

# cursor
.cursor/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Node / app build. `dist/` covers both vite's scratch output under app/ and the
# release folder at the root: a built artifact is not source, and a 1.4 MB
# workbook plus zip committed on every release would grow the clone forever to
# store something `./package.sh` reproduces from any commit in seconds.
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/

# `make report` and `make evidence` output: measured evidence belongs to a run,
# not to the repo. A committed report is a number nobody re-measured; CI
# regenerates both every time. The evidence/ artifacts are learner-specific by
# construction — committing one would hand the next reader someone else's proof.
src/workshops/assistant/*/PORTFOLIO.md
src/workshops/assistant/*/EVIDENCE.md
src/workshops/assistant/*/evals/
src/workshops/assistant/*/evidence/

# Python / uv (lesson build artifacts)
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
uv.lock
# ...except the capstone's. Its Dockerfile installs with `uv sync --frozen`, so that
# lock is an input to the shipped image build rather than a local artifact: without
# it, a clean checkout (CI) and the student ZIP both fail at `COPY ... uv.lock`.
!src/workshops/assistant/after/uv.lock
